{"kind":"stack","id":"s-env","title":"Changing environments and dangers to living things","theme":{"background":"#f4faf1","foreground":"#1d3b22","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"tree"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Environment"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Everything around a living thing, like the air, water, soil, weather and other living things."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1-btn","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"button","id":"c1-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"sun"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Environment change"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"When an environment becomes different, for example through a flood, drought, fire or a new road."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2-btn","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"button","id":"c2-next","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which of these is a change to an environment?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A river floods after heavy rain","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A pond is full of frogs in spring","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A tree grows a new leaf","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Why can a forest fire be dangerous to animals?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"It burns their homes and food","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"It makes the rain fall more often","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"It makes the soil softer for worms","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-d","label":"It helps seeds to sleep","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"What is most likely to harm fish when a river dries up?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"They run out of water to live in","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"They get too much sunshine to swim","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"They grow too big for the pond","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"Which is a danger to living things from a change in weather?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"A long drought with no rain","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"A warm, sunny afternoon","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-c","label":"A light breeze in the garden","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-d","label":"Some clouds in the sky","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"Why might a bird be in danger when its woodland is cut down?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"It loses the trees where it nests and finds food","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"It gets too many leaves to carry","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"It has to swim across the sea","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"A new road is planned through a wood where hedgehogs live. What should the class do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Tell the council about the hedgehogs","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Say nothing and let the road be built","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"The council agrees to move the road. The hedgehogs keep their wood and their homes are safe."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-t","content":"The road is built. The hedgehogs lose their homes and food, and fewer of them survive."},{"type":"button","id":"c10-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-q","content":"What can living things do when their environment changes?"},{"type":"button","id":"c11-a","label":"Adapt, move or sometimes die","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-b","label":"Change their colour to match the rain","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-c","label":"Always stay exactly the same","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c12","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c12-h","content":"Well done, you finished the set!"},{"type":"text","id":"c12-m","content":"Environments can change, and living things must adapt, move or be harmed. Keep looking at the world around you."}],"actions":[]}}
